<title>UK: Virtuality shares suspended temporarily.</title>
<headline>Virtuality shares suspended temporarily.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British virtual reality systems company Virtuality Group Plc were suspended temporarily on Thursday at 68-1/2p pending clarification of the company's financial position, the London stock exchange said.</p>
<p>Last month Virtuality shares gained strongly on talk that Dutch electronics group Philips Electronics was interested in making a bid for the company.</p>
<p>Philips declined to comment on the speculation at that time. It said it had a small stake in Virtuality and was in product-related talks.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
